# SmartMed subagent auto-delegation

For SmartMed tasks, **delegate to project subagents** in `.cursor/agents/` instead of doing all work inline. Do not wait for the user to name a subagent.

## Routing

| Task type | Subagent |
|-----------|----------|
| New feature, refactor, layer placement, architecture review | `smartmed-architect` |
| Forms, Designer.cs, grids, dashboards, theme, UI events | `winforms-ui` |
| SQL, schema, migrations, repositories, `SmartMed/Data/` | `sql-repository` |
| Services, validation, orders, stock, discounts, expiry | `business-logic` |
| Review, test plan, verify, find bugs, before submit | `qa-testing` |
| Report, diagrams, essay, `Docs/`, requirements text | `documentation` |

## Multi-layer features

1. Delegate to `smartmed-architect` first for a brief layer plan.
2. Delegate implementation in parallel when independent: `sql-repository`, `business-logic`, `winforms-ui`.
3. After non-trivial changes, delegate `qa-testing` in the background (`is_background: true`).

## Rules

- Match subagent scope — do not ask `winforms-ui` to write SQL or `sql-repository` to build forms.
- Prefer subagents over generic `explore` for SmartMed layer work.
- Tell the user which subagent(s) were used in one short line at the start of the reply.
